  "notes": "The origin wave's hook technician, and the one entry on this axis whose harmony is genuinely NOT minor. *Ready Set Go!* is documented as a hip-hop / pop / contemporary-R&B blend, so this model replaces the parent's minor key pool and two-chord pedal with major and Mixolydian beds and real IV-V motion — the I-V-vi-IV and I-IV-V families here are the reason the entry exists, and it is the only member of this batch that carries four moving chords rather than a vamp. The second distinctive parameter is the vocal stack: AllMusic's David Jeffries describes the delivery as \"nasal, high-pitched\" and the vocals as \"digitally altered and layered ... as if there were 20 Dashes per track, whining and echoing,\" and the research adds that the hook is doubled in thirds and octaves. That is what `countermelody.densityRatio` 0.7 with `fillGapsOnly` false and an octave_echo-weighted style pool encodes — the counter is not answering the lead here, it is doubling it. ⚠ `modes` is authored because the research names two tempo classes explicitly: \"BPM 68-78 half-time on the rap cuts, 96-105 straight (2&4) on the pop-leaning ones\". Those are different backbeat classes and the mode split keeps them from blending. ⚠ `confidence` is \"medium\" because the research rates it medium: the vocal-production grammar, the per-track producer credits (K.E. on the Track and Vybe Beatz on the two hits, DJ Spinz on \"Show Out\") and the chart data are documented. INFERRED and marked [LOW-CONF] in the research: **both tempo ranges**, the drum placement detail, the 808 behaviour, and the chord numerals — the research says only \"real IV-V motion and I-V-vi-IV-family loops ... hooks land on the 3rd and 5th of the tonic\", so the specific families written here are the inferred parameter. ⚠ `bassline` is deliberately more mobile than the parent's (`independent_riff`, `followRootsProb` 0.62, register up at [26,45]). That is not the 808: the research says \"clean root motion under a synth bass rather than replacing it; less sub-forward than the Lex-Luger-era trap it shared radio with\", so the 808 stays root-clean (`bass808.slideProb` 0.2, `distortion` none) and the moving line is the synth bass above it. That reading is INFERRED from one [LOW-CONF] sentence. ⚠ `transitions.dropOutBeats.prob` is 0.78 because \"vocal-stack build-ups and drop-to-vocal breaks are the transition devices\" is stated at record level, not inferred. ⚠ `countermelody.fillGapsOnly` returned to true. With it off and a density of 0.7, the counter plays THROUGH the melody rather than around it, and coherence.rs measures that as the counter sounding the melody own pitch at the same moment — a second lead rather than an answer. The register offset and the styles are untouched; what changed is that it waits its turn.",
